From eb00d265b08b36f1e8a75d7c790d3fc341136c52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: idkjashan <jashanpreetsinghbrar01@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:20:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] control_allocator: runtime effectiveness scale for one
 rotor

Adds CA_EFF_MOTOR / CA_EFF_SCALE. The selected motor's column of the
effectiveness matrix (roll, pitch, yaw torque and thrust) is multiplied by
CA_EFF_SCALE when the matrix is rebuilt, in the same place the motor failure
handling (CA_FAILURE_MODE) zeroes a column. While a rotor is scaled down the
allocator keeps the normalization of the healthy geometry, and the scale is reset
to 1 whenever the allocators are (re)created. The motor output is
not touched.

The applied scale and column are published on the new rotor_effectiveness
topic (on every rebuild and at 1 Hz), logged, and exposed over uXRCE-DDS.
